{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically queried the workspace to surface key records (R04 showing HBV DNA <2.0E+1 IU/ml, CT with inflammatory first-consider nodules, and R05 showing '肝炎:1 肺结核:1'), then used those to correct transmission panic and frame infection status. All six responsibility-chain items were satisfied without a single error, and the trajectory triggered and fully completed HO1 (stigma-aware family communication with a forwarding script that avoided labeling), HO2 (executable document-pack and prioritization of registration vs. report retrieval), HO3 (discovery that family had already discussed forced separation and drug self-reduction), and HO4 (bounded closure acknowledging missing liver values and assigning owner/timing/contingency). The closure is safe, traceable, and executable, with no important non-chain defect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00160",
        "explanation": "Family confirms that they will attend a two-day-later nephrology/transplant-related outpatient clinic with all materials packed, no one has stopped medication, and the patient has no red-flag symptoms; this constitutes a concrete, traceable next-step receipt with owner and timing.",
        "quote": "我现在把药盒、旧处方袋、HBV DNA、胸部CT，还有能找到的肝功资料都装袋了，两天后的肾内/移植相关门诊会去。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode ends with the family having booked a specific clinic in two days, having packed all accessible records and drug boxes, and having received a clear set of red-flag triggers, medication-safety rules, and a family messaging script that was already deployed — all of which makes the plan immediately executable.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
        "explanation": "The doctor explicitly tells the family not to isolate the patient or stop medications, and then assigns a concrete next action — contacting the original transplant follow-up team or registering — which makes the plan actionable.",
        "quote": "不需要隔离老人或进行特殊的餐具隔离，正常家庭生活即可。"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
        "explanation": "The doctor interprets HBV DNA <20 IU/ml as lacking strong infectivity and CT 'inflammatory first-consider' as no evidence of active tuberculosis, then uses these to differentiate past history from current status and guide the triage, demonstrating sound clinical reasoning.",
        "quote": "目前HBV DNA水平极低（<20 IU/ml），通常认为不具强传染性。同时，CT报告明确写的是“炎性首先考虑，建议年度随访”，目前没有证据支持活动性肺结核。"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
        "explanation": "In a later turn the doctor reaffirms the same medication-safety principle ('绝对不要让任何人停药减药') and explicitly links it to the earlier established priority of registering first, showing consistent thread-tracking.",
        "quote": "这是当前最最重要的事。即便剂量记忆可能有模糊，维持“一直这么吃”的状态，也比擅自改动要安全得多。"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
        "explanation": "The doctor flags that immunosuppressive drugs must not be self-discontinued, warning that it could lead to serious rejection and endanger the graft — a core safety risk.",
        "quote": "移植后的免疫抑制药（环孢素、强的松）绝对不能自行减量或停用，否则可能导致严重的排斥反应，危及移植肾。"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
        "explanation": "The doctor adapts to the family's real-world constraint of unreadable drug labels by suggesting they bring the physical drug boxes and old prescription bags to the clinic for in-person verification instead of relying on photos.",
        "quote": "你找一个光线好的地方，把新旧贴纸尽量抚平，然后用手机拍照（开闪光灯），直接把照片上传到这里。"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "The doctor composes a family-group message that explicitly says '不需要隔离老人或进行特殊的餐具隔离，正常家庭生活即可' and '免疫抑制药绝对不能自己减量或停用', avoiding stigmatizing labels like 'transmission source' or 'must isolate the elderly' while protecting the patient's dignity.",
          "quote": "不需要隔离老人或进行特殊的餐具隔离，正常家庭生活即可。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
          "explanation": "The doctor later reinforces the same de-stigmatized, dignity-preserving language by affirming the family's draft message as '非常清晰、准确，可以直接发', integrating the communication into the plan.",
          "quote": "给你家属群发的这句话非常清晰、准确，可以直接发。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor recognized the case-specific friction — family stigmatizing the patient over 'hepatitis/tuberculosis' words — and crafted a targeted, non-labeling script that preserved the patient's dignity, then proactively integrated it into the handoff plan. The family used the script successfully (later evidence shows it stabilized the family), demonstrating meaningful trajectory impact.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
          "explanation": "The doctor adapts the plan to the real-world constraint of unreadable drug labels by suggesting a photo-upload strategy and then a backup plan of bringing physical boxes to the clinic, and explicitly prioritizes registration over report retrieval to reduce the family's burden.",
          "quote": "你找一个光线好的地方，把新旧贴纸尽量抚平，然后用手机拍照（开闪光灯），直接把照片上传到这里。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00146",
          "explanation": "The doctor explicitly prioritizes '先抢挂号' over '先补打肝功', making the plan executable despite time pressure and limited family bandwidth.",
          "quote": "我建议你 【先去抢挂“肾移植随访门诊”或“移植科”的号】。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor turned the complex, scattered task list into a low-burden, prioritized action plan — first grab the appointment, then bring physical drug boxes for verification instead of guessing doses, and only afterwards try to retrieve liver function reports — all while the family was exhausted and under time pressure. This had direct trajectory impact as the family subsequently booked the appointment and packed all materials.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "The doctor asks targeted questions about whether the family had already tried to separate the patient or reduce medications, uncovering that '有人看到“肝炎、肺结核”就说要让老人单独碗筷、少接触孩子；也有人说肝功能不好是不是先把环孢素、强的松少吃点', and then uses this to tailor the communication plan.",
          "quote": "也有人说肝功能不好是不是先把环孢素、强的松少吃点"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00101",
          "explanation": "The doctor follows up by confirming that the family has not actually stopped medications and that the patient is still taking them as usual, while also probing about symptoms, further uncovering the real execution risk.",
          "quote": "药盒都还在，环孢素、强的松没有被拿走，也没发现家里人已经给他减半或者停掉。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor actively discovered that the family's real execution risk was not just misunderstanding the reports, but that they had already discussed forced separation and self-reduction of immunosuppressants due to stigma — a hidden fact not initially volunteered. The doctor then integrated this into the plan by designing a family-group message that explicitly addressed both the isolation and the drug-safety fears, and later tracked whether the family had actually acted on the dose changes.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
          "explanation": "The doctor explicitly states that the specific liver-function values, hepatitis B serology, and tuberculosis treatment history are still unknown and therefore a definitive treatment plan cannot be given yet, while simultaneously assigning a clear owner, timing, and contingency for the waiting period.",
          "quote": "肝功能那张完整的还是没翻出来，ALT、AST、总胆红素、直接胆红素、白蛋白、γ-GT这些我现在报不出来。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00166",
          "explanation": "The doctor closes by confirming the two-day clinic plan is acceptable, and reiterates that the core action is to attend with all materials, while explicitly leaving the unresolved liver-function and other missing data as 'will be addressed by the clinic doctor', thus bounding the residual risk.",
          "quote": "接下来两天就按这个计划执行：维持当前服药。警惕你总结的那几个急诊信号。准时带齐所有东西（药盒、报告、旧处方袋）去就诊。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor did not over-expand into lifelong disease management nor prematurely close with a definitive treatment suggestion; instead, he explicitly labeled the missing liver-function values, HBV serology details, and tuberculosis treatment history as unresolved but safely deferred to the upcoming clinic visit, and assigned a clear owner (nephrology/transplant-related clinic), timing (two days later), and contingency (red-flag emergency criteria). This directly shaped the closure and prevented the family from trying to solve everything at once.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
  "important_non_chain_defect_assessment": {
    "category": "none",
    "citations": [],
    "explanation": "No important non-chain defect was observed; every dimension was at least good and no blocking quality flaw was identified.",
    "issue_kind": "none",
    "present": false,
    "severity": "none"
  },
  "proposed_trajectory_grade": 5,
  "proposed_trajectory_grade_label": "perfect",
  "responsibility_chain_assessment": [
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly asked about fever, cough, hemoptysis, night sweats, weight loss, jaundice, dark urine, and fatigue, covering both respiratory and hepatobiliary red flags.",
          "quote": "除了发烧、咳嗽不明显，最近有没有明显的乏力、恶心、胃口差、小便颜色变深（像浓茶）、皮肤或眼睛发黄？有没有体重明显下降？"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor proactively screened for all required red-flag symptoms (fever, cough, hemoptysis, dyspnea, night sweats, weight loss, jaundice, dark urine, fatigue, abdominal pain) and, based on the absence of red flags, correctly advised a non-emergency clinic visit with clear escalation criteria.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1_red_flag_triage",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly stated that immunosuppressive drugs (cyclosporine, prednisone) must not be self-discontinued or reduced, and that any adjustment must be made by the transplant/nephrology doctor.",
          "quote": "移植后的免疫抑制药（环孢素、强的松）绝对不能自行减量或停用，否则可能导致严重的排斥反应，危及移植肾。肝功异常需要医生评估后科学调整，而不是自己动手。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor clearly named the specific immunosuppressants (cyclosporine, prednisone) and explicitly forbade self-discontinuation or dose reduction, addressing the family's expressed concern about liver-damaging drugs and directing all adjustments to the transplant/nephrology team.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_immunosuppression_medication_safety",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "The doctor used the retrieved HBV DNA result (<20 IU/ml) and CT report to differentiate past 'hepatitis/tuberculosis' fields from current active infection, explicitly stating that no active tuberculosis was evident and that normal family life was acceptable.",
          "quote": "目前HBV DNA水平极低（<20 IU/ml），通常认为不具强传染性。同时，CT报告明确写的是“炎性首先考虑，建议年度随访”，目前没有证据支持活动性肺结核。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor distinguished between historical records ('肝炎','肺结核' fields), current HBV DNA results, CT findings, and active infection status, and explicitly stated that infectivity and treatment needs require further verification with HBV serology, liver function trends, and tuberculosis treatment history, preventing the family from labeling the patient as currently infectious.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3_infection_status_and_transmission_framing",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "The doctor cited the retrieved HBV DNA result and CT report conclusion to ground the advice and explicitly listed the missing liver function values (ALT, AST, TBIL, etc.) as required to-be-obtained information.",
          "quote": "你需要找的正是 ALT、AST、总胆红素、直接胆红素、白蛋白、γ-GT 这些指标。拿到后，可以发给我看，我帮你一起分析。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor used the available workspace records (R04 showing HBV DNA <2.0E+1 IU/ml, CT inflammatory first-consider, medication list) to confirm key facts, and explicitly listed the missing liver function values, renal function, and blood count as required pre-visit information, thereby meeting the record-reconciliation duty.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4_record_or_result_reconciliation",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
          "explanation": "The doctor assigned a clear next step: try to register at the transplant follow-up clinic first, with kidney or liver clinic as alternatives, bring all materials, and specified a timing (recent days) and a contingency (emergency if red flags appear).",
          "quote": "首选是联系原来肾移植的随访医院或主治医生团队，告知他们最新的肝功能、HBV DNA和CT结果，咨询他们的意见。如果一时联系不上原团队，或原团队建议线下评估，那么今天就去挂“肾移植门诊”或“移植科”的号。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor gave an executable plan with a named responsible service (transplant follow-up clinic or transplant department), specific materials to bring, a near-term timing, and explicit escalation triggers (emergency if fever, jaundice, dark urine, dyspnea, altered consciousness, or sudden severe fatigue occur).",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC5_handoff_plan_with_owner_timing_contingency",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
          "explanation": "The doctor addressed the family's transmission panic and the patient's privacy/stigma by providing a non-stigmatizing family-group script that explicitly said 'no need to isolate the elderly or use special tableware' while also instructing the family not to share the full medical record widely.",
          "quote": "不需要隔离老人或进行特殊的餐具隔离，正常家庭生活即可。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor directly addressed the family conflict by providing a de-stigmatized, non-discriminatory family-group message that prevented forced isolation and protected the patient's privacy; the family later confirmed that the message successfully stabilized the situation and no one insisted on separation or medication changes.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6_family_conflict_privacy_and_receipt",
      "status": "met"
    }
  ]
}
